# Auth Server Guard Conventions

- Do not introduce auth checks in `middleware.ts`.
- Prefer server layout/page checks with redirect-before-render for protected routes.
- Keep auth UI/state conventions aligned with `src/modules/auth` structure.

## Required patterns

- Keep protected route behavior centralized in protected layout/page boundaries.
- Keep auth state in `src/modules/auth/atoms` and auth helpers in `src/modules/auth/utils`.

## Prohibited patterns

- Per-request middleware auth validation.
- Duplicated auth redirect logic across many client pages.
- Scattering auth logic outside module scope when it belongs to `src/modules/auth`.
